{
  "file": "module4",
  "page": 51,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        67.39069366455078,
        527.4398193359375,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "recent years in identifying more efficacious, safer medicines and shorter treatment regimens. Since",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.1793212890625,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "the 1990s, WHO has regularly evaluated evidence on the use of specific drug compositions and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        92.51471710205078,
        524.4899291992188,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "(2, 9–16) combinations of regimens of different durations  . Historically, patients with certain drug-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        106.99073028564453,
        527.2088623046875,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "resistance patterns were often treated for 20 months or longer. In 2016, a standardized shorter",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        527.5618286132812,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "treatment regimen (9–12 months) was recommended for patients with MDR/RR-TB strains not resistant",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.949935913085938,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        133.3907012939453,
        527.1306762695312,
        147.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "to fluoroquinolones or second-line injectable agents, although longer regimens (18–20 months)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        146.59071350097656,
        527.3134155273438,
        161.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "continued to be an option for patients who were not eligible for the shorter option. Subsequent",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        159.7907257080078,
        527.4365234375,
        174.2337188720703
      ],
      "text": "modifications to these treatment regimens led WHO to assess new evidence, which in turn resulted",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        172.99073791503906,
        527.50244140625,
        187.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "in revised recommendations, balancing the effectiveness and harms of new regimens or modifications",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.972765922546387,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        186.1907501220703,
        200.80252075195312,
        200.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "of recommended regimens.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.4102172851562,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "Interest in reducing the duration of treatment for MDR/RR-TB has driven several initiatives in recent",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        219.81874084472656,
        527.4241333007812,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "(17–22) years to treat patients with shorter regimens under programmatic and trial conditions  . When",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        234.29469299316406,
        527.462646484375,
        248.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "used in carefully selected patients with MDR/RR-TB who have not been previously exposed or do not",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.993098258972168,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        247.4947052001953,
        527.4025268554688,
        261.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "have additional resistance to second-line medicines, these regimens can achieve relapse-free cure in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        259.418701171875,
        527.4282836914062,
        275.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "(17, 21) about 80% of cases or more, even under programmatic conditions  . In 2016, on the basis of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        273.89459228515625,
        527.4312133789062,
        288.3376159667969
      ],
      "text": "data from observational studies of the standardized shorter regimens in various countries in Africa",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        287.0947265625,
        527.5266723632812,
        301.5377502441406
      ],
      "text": "and Asia, WHO for the first time recommended a standardized 9–12-month shorter MDR-TB regimen",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.970561027526855,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        299.0186767578125,
        527.4371337890625,
        314.7377014160156
      ],
      "text": "(16) for eligible patients  . In 2018, following the results of a trial – the Standard Treatment Regimen of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        313.49468994140625,
        527.5272827148438,
        327.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "Anti-tuberculosis Drugs for Patients with MDR-TB (STREAM) Stage 1 trial – a revised recommendation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.979331016540527,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        326.6947021484375,
        527.4518432617188,
        341.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "on the use of a shorter MDR-TB regimen was released, following an evidence assessment and a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        339.89471435546875,
        527.4002075195312,
        354.3377380371094
      ],
      "text": "ranking of benefits and harms attributed to specific drugs; the revision included a recommendation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        351.8186950683594,
        432.2967834472656,
        367.5377197265625
      ],
      "text": "(2) to replace the injectable agent, kanamycin (or capreomycin), with amikacin  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.7986145019531,
        527.39794921875,
        389.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "Evidence of permanent effects attributed to the toxicity of injectable agents have prompted further",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        387.99859619140625,
        527.3792724609375,
        402.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "advances in the development of new treatments such as shorter injectable-sparing regimens.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.1986083984375,
        527.4991455078125,
        415.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "Bedaquiline was the first new medicine to be added to the group of available second-line TB medicines.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.94486141204834,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        414.39862060546875,
        527.3287353515625,
        428.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "In 2013, WHO issued interim guidance for using bedaquiline with other WHO-recommended MDR-TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.960780143737793,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        427.5986022949219,
        527.4002685546875,
        442.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "treatments. Bedaquiline gradually became a staple drug in the treatment of DR-TB, initially featuring",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        440.7986145019531,
        527.4454956054688,
        455.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "as an add-on agent in the longer regimens for MDR/RR-TB and then becoming a Group A medicine",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        453.99859619140625,
        527.1482543945312,
        468.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "along with Fluoroquinolones and Linezolid. In 2019, South Africa’s Department of Health shared",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        467.1986083984375,
        527.4268188476562,
        481.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "with WHO observational data on an all-oral bedaquiline-containing shorter regimen of 9 months",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        480.39862060546875,
        527.4288330078125,
        494.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "duration. That regimen was reviewed and has been recommended by WHO since 2019, with the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        493.5986022949219,
        524.51611328125,
        508.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "following combination of medicines: bedaquiline (used for 6 months), in combination with levofloxacin/",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.95214557647705,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        506.798583984375,
        527.1259765625,
        521.2415771484375
      ],
      "text": "moxifloxacin, ethionamide, ethambutol, isoniazid (high-dose), pyrazinamide and clofazimine for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        519.9985961914062,
        527.4124145507812,
        534.4415893554688
      ],
      "text": "4 months (with the possibility of extending to 6 months if the patient remains sputum smear positive",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        533.1986083984375,
        527.5507202148438,
        547.6416015625
      ],
      "text": "at the end of 4 months); followed by 5 months of treatment with levofloxacin/moxifloxacin, clofazimine,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.95837116241455,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        546.3986206054688,
        485.8377990722656,
        560.8416137695312
      ],
      "text": "ethambutol and pyrazinamide (4–6 Bdq[6]-Lfx[Mfx]-Eto-E-Z-Hh-Cfz / 5 Lfx[Mfx]-Cfz-Z-E).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        568.1026000976562,
        527.4113159179688,
        582.5455932617188
      ],
      "text": "The pressing need for more effective treatment regimens for patients with extensive drug resistance,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        581.302490234375,
        527.59814453125,
        595.7454833984375
      ],
      "text": "including fluoroquinolone resistance and more extensive drug-resistance profiles, has been the driver",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.98488998413086,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        594.5026245117188,
        527.5850830078125,
        608.9456176757812
      ],
      "text": "for several studies and initiatives to test more effective and novel treatment regimens, including",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        607.70263671875,
        527.3991088867188,
        622.1456298828125
      ],
      "text": "newer and repurposed medicines. One of the first studies was the Nix-TB study, conducted by the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        620.902587890625,
        527.375,
        635.3455810546875
      ],
      "text": "TB Alliance. The Nix-TB study was a one-arm, Phase 3, open-label observational cohort study that",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        634.1025390625,
        527.4312133789062,
        648.5455322265625
      ],
      "text": "assessed the safety, efficacy, tolerability and pharmacokinetic properties of a 6-month bedaquiline,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        647.302490234375,
        527.4146118164062,
        661.7454833984375
      ],
      "text": "pretomanid and linezolid (BPaL) treatment regimen, extendable to 9 months for those who missed",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        660.5026245117188,
        527.4199829101562,
        674.9456176757812
      ],
      "text": "doses, or remained culture positive or reverted from culture negative to positive between months 4",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        672.4266357421875,
        527.4003295898438,
        688.1456298828125
      ],
      "text": "(23) and 6 of treatment  . The study was conducted between 2014 and 2019 at three study sites, all in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        686.902587890625,
        527.4488525390625,
        701.3455810546875
      ],
      "text": "South Africa, with the first patient enrolled in April 2015. The Nix-TB study contributed evidence to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        700.1025390625,
        527.442138671875,
        714.5455322265625
      ],
      "text": "WHO that was reviewed by the GDG in November 2019 and gave rise to the recommendation for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        713.302490234375,
        493.1033630371094,
        727.7454833984375
      ],
      "text": "the use of the BPaL regimen in pre-XDR-TB patients, under operational research conditions.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        735.0065307617188,
        527.5894775390625,
        749.4495239257812
      ],
      "text": "In preparation for the 2022 guidelines update, WHO/GTB received data from another trial – the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        748.2064819335938,
        527.4474487304688,
        762.6494750976562
      ],
      "text": "Newer and Emerging Treatment for MDR/RR-TB (NExT) trial – which was a Phase 2–3 open-label",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        352.018798828125,
        801.0170288085938,
        554.0401611328125,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "Chapter 2 Drug-resistant TB treatment: Introduction 37",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}